    "updated_at": "2026-06-05T10:08:50Z",
    "body": "Looking into this a bit more, `pagehide` should also fire:\n```js\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<body>\n<script>\nlet frame = document.createElement(\"iframe\");\ndocument.body.appendChild(frame);\nlet doc = frame.contentDocument;\nlet win = frame.contentWindow;\nwin.addEventListener(\"pagehide\", () => console.log(\"pagehide\"));\nconsole.log(doc.visibilityState);\n\nframe.remove();\nconsole.log(doc.visibilityState);\n</script>\n```\n\nMy current guess is that the removal steps for elements with nested navigables should also [unload the document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#unload-a-document) somewhere, but I haven't checked in with implementations enough to confidently make that change right now.",
